Contra Indigo (2010)


Overview


Contra Indigo was a band formed in Bandung, West Java, Indonesia, bringing
together musicians with a shared passion for groove-based music that blends
elements of pop, jazz, funk, and contemporary band sounds. For Metta
Legita, this project represents an important early chapter in her musical
journey as a pianist and performer in Indonesia.


Artistic Concept


The music of Contra Indigo focused on energetic grooves, expressive
ensemble playing, and jazz-influenced harmonies. Through collaborative
arrangements and dynamic interaction between instruments, the band created
a vibrant sound that combined rhythmic drive with melodic creativity.


Band & Musical Journey


The group featured musicians from Bandung, including Bubu Anggraeni
(vocal), Taufik Eka (bass), Yuriandra Bayu (drums), Metta Legita
(keyboard), and Keke Kandrianta (guitar), along with several guest
musicians. During its active years, Contra Indigo performed at numerous
venues and festivals across Indonesia, including 5 times appearances at the
renowned Java Jazz Festival.


The band=E2=80=99s album received a nomination at the Anugerah Musik Indone=
sia,
recognizing the group=E2=80=99s contribution to Indonesia=E2=80=99s contemp=
orary music
scene.


A Musical Chapter


Although the band is no longer active today, Contra Indigo remains a
meaningful part of Metta Legita=E2=80=99s artistic history. The project rep=
resents
a formative period of collaboration, performance, and musical exploration
that helped shape her path as a pianist and composer.

